 r←Test_Misc_037(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;msg;folder;target
⍝ Exercise `ParseDependencySetting` with valid settings: split into folder and target, no message.
⍝ This is the control for Test_Misc_038.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 ⍝ Empty: no such folder
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'##.Cider.ParseDependencySetting''
 →T.PassesIf(0=≢msg)∧(0=≢folder)∧0=≢target

 ⍝ No target namespace: packages go into the project space
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'##.Cider.ParseDependencySetting'tatin-packages'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'tatin-packages'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢target

 (msg folder target)←'dependencies_dev.tatin'##.Cider.ParseDependencySetting'tatin-packages_dev=TestCases'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'tatin-packages_dev'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'TestCases'≡target

 ⍝ A target below a child of the project space
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.nuget'##.Cider.ParseDependencySetting'nuget-packages=Foo.Goo'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'nuget-packages'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'Foo.Goo'≡target

 ⍝ A folder that is not a direct child of the project folder
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.nuget'##.Cider.ParseDependencySetting'deps/nuget=Goo'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'deps/nuget'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'Goo'≡target

 ⍝ A blank inside a folder name is fine
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.tatin'##.Cider.ParseDependencySetting'my packages=Foo'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢msg
 →T.PassesIf'my packages'≡folder
 →T.PassesIf'Foo'≡target

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
